{"id": "DfQzRWwTuPX", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does the Gita say “be like a TORTOISE”? 🐢📱 Watch till the end… and then look up from your phone.\n\nBhagavad Gita 2.58:\n“As a tortoise draws in its limbs, one who draws the senses in from what pulls at them stands firm in wisdom.”\n\nThe tortoise doesn’t fight the world, and it doesn’t run away from it. When something pulls at it, it simply draws in, stays calm, and comes back out when it chooses. The Gita calls this a steady mind (sthita-prajña). Krishna gave Arjuna this picture long before phones existed, and it has never fit better.\n\nNext time your phone buzzes, try being the tortoise. 🐢\n\n👨‍👩‍👧 Watch it with your kids, or send it to someone who needs to look up today.\n💬 Comment 🐢 if you’re trying one phone-free evening this week.\n📚 More stories for kids, rooted in our scriptures: the Navadurga Set is out now · link in bio (rishikatha.com)\n\n#BhagavadGita #GitaWisdom #Krishna #MoralStories #StoriesForKids KidsStories PhoneAddiction DigitalDetox Mindfulness Parenting SanatanDharma HinduScriptures AnimatedStory RishiKatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793672684, "like_count": 73, "comment_count": 1, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-2166501340718130a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 74.944, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQOD5azQdKzJweux2aOHU7lDi99fPBW0xJuqB3GBYeSHrfN2s520O04JY0Wo1gDpkGgkaogwf9RKBM4qN-OP2LBGq8cToRBYyhLEHXA.mp4?_nc_cat=106&_nc_oc=AdpfUdyh9V-yOMaO620wlAloynZQRwlHTgpaqmUO_NSklkatPt6swQ9D7zPmPLhwbH2LAEPzjy_c4lgT20N_k2-2&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=iF3K-kC7_IkQ7kNvwG_AR6B&&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=Mu-llWeGyLGITDH49r-Fyg&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQT2C3J0vxn8ZK_2T